+	// ACVR: a scripted headset gun: ACVR_RAY="t:px:py:dist:ox:oy:oz:trigger;..." from game time t (until the
+	// next entry) aims from a muzzle at ox, oy, oz (metres from the head, y up, -z ahead) at the point dist metres
+	// along the eye ray through DC pixel px, py (the stock 640 x 480 framing; outside it: past the frame), with
+	// the trigger held (1), not held (0) or not held and the decision only logged (2, a probe). It runs the headset's own gun decision (xr_host.cpp testGunRay) on the
+	// frames the renderer draws, so it needs vr.Reproject and the renderer keeping them (gles.cpp). Use it in
+	// place of ACVR_GUN.
+	{
+		struct RayStep { double at; float px, py, dist, ox, oy, oz; int trigger; };
+		static std::vector<RayStep> rays;
